The thing to keep in mind is that all 3 of these classes are
combat-oriented from the start.  Valks, however, are (IMHO) the easiest
class to win with just because of the Quest.  The Samaurai quest is a
pain because you pretty much need one or two "oLS handy before you can
be sure you won't randomly get instakilled, and both the Samurai and
Barbarian quest artifacts are worthless: the Samurai one is a 2-handed
weapon when it's better to wield FB and a katana and not have to worry
about cursing anyway, and the Barbarian one confers stealth, controlled
levitation, and (most pathetic of all) to-hit and damage bonuses if you
want to chuck your quest artifact at things.  I mean, seriously.

On the other hand, Valks have a cakewalk quest (I've never had a lvl 14
valk go below half health on it; the hardest part of the whole quest is
not getting crushed by the drawbridge), with a sweet quest artifact
(1/2 physical damage etc.), meaning that if you can get a valk to level
14, you pretty much get a pile of free bonuses that no other class gets
(well, I guess Wizards are a close second, with the awesome Eye of the
Aethiopica as the reward for beating some random loser, albeit a random
loser with a cool-looking tile...).

Basically, that means that if you want a combat-oriented character for
your first ascension, play Valkyries.  If you want a 'caster go for
Wizards, for not only the starting equipment but also the spell skills
and, of course, the only Quest which is comparable to Valkyries' as far
as difficulty : payoff ratio goes.

